, and 5.11% .", "type": "ListItem"}, {"bbox": [16.734375, 454.0078125, 673.2359619140625, 474.4371643066406], "text": "(3) Issued in August 2017, effective interest rates of the 2020, 2023, 2024, 2027, 2037, 2047, and 2057 Notes were 2.16% , 2.56% , 2.95% , 3.25% , 3.94% , 4.13% , and 4.33% .", "type": "ListItem"}, {"bbox": [15.837890625, 475.27734375, 772.4103393554688, 504.8121643066406], "text": "(4) Consists of $872 million of 2025 Notes issued in December 2017 in exchange for notes assumed in connection with the acquisition of Whole Foods Market and $128 million of 2025 Notes issued by Whole Foods Market that did not participate in our December 2017 exchange offer. The effective interest rate of the 2025 Notes was 3.02% .", "type": "ListItem"}, {"bbox": [15.5390625, 513.5625, 931.8795776367188, 583.7871398925781], "text": "Interest on the Notes issued in 2012 is payable semi-annually in arrears in May and November . Interest on the Notes issued in 2014 is payable semi-annually in arrears in June and December . Interest on the Notes issued in 2017 is payable semi-annually in arrears in February and August. Interest on the 2025 Notes is payable semi-annually in arrears in June and December. We may redeem the Notes at any time in whole, or from time to time, in part at specified redemption prices. We are not subject to any financial covenants under the Notes. The proceeds from the November 2012 and December 2014 Notes were used for general corporate purposes. The proceeds from the August 2017 Notes were used to fund the consideration for the acquisition of Whole Foods Market, to repay the 1.200% Notes due November 2017, and for general corporate purposes. The estimated fair value of the Notes was approximately $8.7 billion and $25.7 billion as of December 31, 2016 and 2017 , which is based on quoted prices for our debt as of those dates.", "type": "Text"}, {"bbox": [17.549999237060547, 592.453125, 744.7567138671875, 632.671875], "text": "In October 2016, we entered into a $500 million secured revolving credit facility with a lender that is secured by certain seller receivables , which we subsequently increased to $600 million and may from time to time increase in the future subject to lender approval (the \"Credit Facility\"). The Credit Facility is available for a term of three years , bears interest at the London interbank offered rate (\" LIBOR \") plus 1.65% , and has a commitment fee of 0.50% on the undrawn portion. There was $495", "type": "Text"}, {"bbox": [299.724609375, 643.88671875, 309.82501220703125, 653.3121643066406], "text": "", "type": "PageFooter"}], "doc_id": "AMAZON_2017_10K.pdf", "page_index": 55, "pdf_path": "/mmfs1/data/group/ems036/lxu/mpvrdu/.data/mmlongbench/documents/AMAZON_2017_10K.pdf", "source": "marker"}